infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One big tsconfig vs project references: what each save re-checks
  desc Same 200k-line monorepo — composite + tsc -b turn a 90s full re-check into a per-project incremental build
  compares
    - label One big tsconfig
      children
        - label 90s type-check on every save
          desc One config re-checks all 200k lines whenever any single file changes
        - label A one-line edit invalidates everything
          desc No package boundary, so every package is re-analysed together
        - label No .tsbuildinfo reuse
          desc tsc re-hashes the whole program; nothing is skipped
        - label Editor re-checks the whole repo
          desc Language server re-analyses every package on each keystroke
    - label Project references + tsc -b
      children
        - label Edit re-checks only that project
          desc A one-line web edit rebuilds just web, reusing cached core and ui
        - label Builds dependencies before dependents
          desc tsc -b topo-sorts the reference DAG: core then ui then web
        - label .tsbuildinfo skips unchanged projects
          desc Inputs hashed against the cache; a dependent rebuilds only on a public .d.ts change
        - label Editor checks one project in isolation
          desc Each composite project is type-checked alone, not the whole monorepo
theme
  palette #f59e0b #14b8a6
